  port #1 configured state 0x5001, IPv4 ..... PASS         (0x0000 -> port1.0.1 "administrative state is
                                                            DOWN", "shutdown" in running-config, NSM
                                                            "user shutdown"; 0xf000 reverses all three)
  port #1 PoE configuration 0x5002 .......... UNSUPPORTED  (read and write answer a Modbus exception;
                                                            "show power-inline" -> % Invalid input)
  0x5001 write over global IPv6 ............. PASS         (logged "from fd32:b1f0:dff8:d701::1",
                                                            read back, applied both ways)
  0x5001 write over link-local IPv6 ......... PASS         (logged "from fe80::f667:7041:7dff:3cfc",
                                                            read back, applied both ways)
CAVEAT:  The case's "bit 0 = LED" is the most significant bit on the DUT. The case's literal value
         0x0001 is acknowledged (FC06 echo) and logged "Performed write request", but it has no
         effect and returns no exception, so a client cannot tell from the response that nothing
         was configured. The LED setting is 0x8000, and that write is the one graded.
         Steps 2, 4 and 5 change only the enabled nibble of 0x5001 (0x0000 / 0xf000) on
         port1.0.1, an empty SFP cage with no link: the administrative state is proven. The
         duplex, polarity and speed nibbles were written as auto only and were not varied.

